  "review": "Architect-published monograph pp.3-4, individually compared against native high-resolution source crops. All source black filled core walls, radial partitions and columns are recovered in addition to glass/door/furniture linework. Upper floors follow the many native facade vertices. The former ground envelope was actually the dashed projection of upper floors and has been removed, not rounded into a fictional ground slab.",
  "internalNotes": [
    "来源记录了地面层、九至二十七层的代表性办公层，以及二十八层活动空间；这些图不能被表述为上方公共观景平台的测绘平面。",
    "既有导览停靠点0至4均涉及现行访客入口、最后一段楼梯和屋顶观景方向。它们保留在重建报告中，但由于来源没有访客标注或屋顶平台平面，暂不绑定。",
    "建筑师图纸带有比例尺，但生成模型只保持来源页面单位，不对外提供米制测量。各层独立摆放仅用于显示。",
    "图中没有访客房间编号，因此模型不虚构编号。办公桌和活动座椅仅作为平面细节，不抬升为墙体。",
    "Ground native path 325 is an upper-storey projection, visually confirmed with subpath overlays. It remains dashed detail only; no ground slab is inferred across the low-rise junction or external door openings.",
    "Upper-floor native paths 130 and 40 carry the convex glazing perimeter; original facade samples replace the coarse manual outlines. The floor surface is a display footprint, not a navigable room or published access permission."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "目前只有地面层、九至二十七层的代表性办公层，以及二十八层活动空间。",
    "公共观景平台、游客入口与最后一段楼梯尚未定位；办公空间不代表可参观范围。"
  ],
